{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Stinginess","html":"<article id='an7.10'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Aṅguttara Nikāya 7.10 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Numbered Discourses 7.10 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>1. Dhanavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>1. Wealth </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Macchariyasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stinginess </span></h1></header>\n<p><span class='root'>“Sattimāni, bhikkhave, saṁyojanāni. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Mendicants, there are these seven fetters. </span>\n<span class='root'>Katamāni satta? </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What seven? </span>\n<span class='root'>Anunayasaṁyojanaṁ, paṭighasaṁyojanaṁ, diṭṭhisaṁyojanaṁ, vicikicchāsaṁyojanaṁ, mānasaṁyojanaṁ, issāsaṁyojanaṁ, macchariyasaṁyojanaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The fetters of attraction, aversion, views, doubt, conceit, jealousy, and stinginess. </span>\n<span class='root'>Imāni kho, bhikkhave, satta saṁyojanānī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>These are the seven fetters.” </span></p>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Dasamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Dhanavaggo paṭhamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dve piyāni balaṁ dhanaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Saṅkhittañceva vitthataṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Uggaṁ saṁyojanañceva, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pahānaṁ macchariyena cāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote></article>"}
